body:
Several performance issues in the core game logic: recursive flood fill risking stack overflow on large grids, O(n²) mine placement using linear scan, an unfixable `contextmenu` event listener leak, redundant DOM writes, and a double `neighbourList` iteration in `togetherBack`.

## Changes

- **`nullSpreadBack` (flood fill)** — replaced recursion with iterative BFS queue, eliminating call-stack overflow risk on large open areas
- **`createMineList`** — replaced `Array.find()` duplicate check (O(n) per iteration → O(n²) total) with a `Set` keyed on `"x,y"` for O(1) lookups
- **`addEventListener` / `removeEventListener`** — extracted anonymous `contextmenu` handler into `_preventContextMenu` class property so `removeEventListener` can actually deregister it (previously a no-op, leaking the listener on every game reset)
- **`togetherBack`** — merged two sequential `neighbourList.forEach` passes into one, collecting items into `toOpen[]` during the first pass
- **`setUIState` (Grid)** — removed the redundant `innerHTML = ""` write immediately before setting `innerHTML` to the span content

```js
// Before: O(n²) mine placement
let isResume = MineList.find(i => i.coo.x === tag_x && i.coo.y === tag_y);

// After: O(1) per check
const placedSet = new Set();
const key = `${tag_x},${tag_y}`;
if (!placedSet.has(key)) { placedSet.add(key); ... }
```

```js
// Before: recursive — risks stack overflow
function flood(itemIns) { ... flood(i_ins); }

// After: iterative BFS
const queue = [actionItemIns];
while (queue.length) { const itemIns = queue.shift(); ... }
```

